# Runs of check.sh, or a step of one, whose failure doesn't fail Check on Linux while their issue is
# open (check/quarantine.sh says how). A line lasts 14 days:
# <run>[@<session>] #<issue> <YYYY-MM-DD> [<its FAIL line's start, as the summary shows it>]
# As on Windows, only the memory rows at 10 and 20 tabs fail perf's gate (check/perf.sh), and they
# come out once ilo is within 10 % of Chrome's on Linux, uBlock Origin's process gone with #2111.
perf #2138 2026-11-11 ilo took more than 10 % over Chrome on this runner: memory,
# Under Wayland a click that moves the Library's icon picker to another card also picks the Space
# it was over, so the escape after it closes the Library (#2689).
spaces@wayland #2689 2026-11-13 escape in the card's icon picker closed the Library
